  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Initially electrophilic addition reaction takes place and form alcohol and alkyl bromide. Then Wurtz reaction takes place.</p><p>The Wurtz reaction is a very useful reaction in the fields of organic chemistry and organometallic chemistry for the formation of alkanes. In this reaction, two different alkyl halides are coupled to yield a longer alkane&nbsp;chain with the help of sodium and dry ether solution.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a022e6b2-1d31-4625-8cb1-2707a2e55705.jpeg\" /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4489bb56-95ea-4c15-8d34-d8ebbabea576.jpeg\" /></p>",
